 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law, in relation to authorizing the town of Newburgh,\nOrange county, to establish a road improvement district in the Ridge Hudson\nValley development area",
    "basePrintNo": "S5792",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5792-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §202-c, Town L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5792\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the town law, in relation to authoriz-\ning the town of Newburgh, Orange county, to establish a road improvement\ndistrict in the Ridge Hudson Valley development area\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo enable the Town of Newburgh to create a new road improvement district\nto serve the properties located in the Ridge Hudson Valley development\narea.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Authorizes the Town of Newburgh to establish a special road\nimprovement district.\n\nSection 2: Defines the boundaries of the road improvement district\n\nSection 3: Lists the purpose of the road improvement district.\n\nSection 4: Amends Section 202-c of the town law to add a new subdivision\n11 authorizing the Town of Newburgh to diminish the size of, extend,\nmerge or combine any lighting district or districts in the town.\n\nSection 5: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Ridge Hudson Valley is a proposed mixed-use commercial/residential\ndevelopment located near the junction of 1-84 and the NY State Thruway.\nThe Town of Newburgh has requested this legislation to enable the\ncreation of a special road district that will allow the property owner\nof the Ridge Hudson Valley to undertake road and other improvements\nspecific to the district. The bill also allows the town to modify the\nboundaries of existing lighting districts. Many other municipalities\nhave received similar authorization to modify or dissolve special light-\ning and other service districts.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
