    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 278\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 5792, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the town law, in relation to authorizing the town\n      of Newburgh,  Orange  county,  to  establish  a  road  improvement\n      district in the Ridge Hudson Valley development area\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  amends the Town law to authorize a special taxing district\nfor a specific development project in the Town of Newburgh.\n \n  I continue to steadfastly support local economic development, however,\nheightened scrutiny must be applied to any project requiring creation of\na new governmental entity with taxing  authority.  More  information  is\nrequired  regarding  the  project intended to benefit from this bill and\nthe impact this proposal will have on local taxpayers. Until such infor-\nmation is provided, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 278,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2019
   }
